<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adam Olearius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1599–1671</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adam Olearius was a German scholar in the service of Duke Frederick III of Holstein-Gottorp. He was secretary of the duke's embassy to Muscovy and Safavid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> from 1635 to 1639, and his account of the journey became a widely read description of both countries. He also translated Saadi's Gulistan and oversaw the building of the great Gottorp globe.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adam-olearius.jpg" alt="Adam Olearius" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jürgen Ovens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adam-Olearius.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
